From: iOSPlus10 ios26 port
Subject: [PATCH 0001] non-Apple SoC base for xnu-12377 (from UniXNU-ios26)

Generic changes that let xnu-12377.121.6 build and start on a non-Apple ARMv8/v9 SoC with the PPL-era
open-source pmap and no KDK KernelSupport archive:
- machine_routines_nos.c: source for ml_device_is_prod_fused/siq_init/siq_cpu_init (only in KDK archives)
- link the KDK lib<SoC>.os.<config>.a only when it exists
- CONFIG_APPLE_AMCC option: AMCC read-only-region code only on Apple SoCs
- start.s: Apple per-SoC tunables only with APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY
- apple_arm64_cpu.h includes apple_arm64_regs.h (MPIDR_CORETYPE_*)
- no ml_enable_monitor() without XNU_MONITOR; CleanPoC_DcacheRegion_Force_nopreempt_nohid alias
- pmap.c: no SART/UAT without XNU_MONITOR; pmap_cs lockdown helpers only with PMAP_CS
- pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys: ptoa() (64-bit PA; = slop 0126 of the iOS 16 port)
- -v gives the text console; boot-args are logged
- device-tree panic region: size checks

Source: UniXNU-ios26 patches/xnu-12377 (01-kernel-support-source, source-machine-layer [without the
MASTER.arm64.bcm2837 hunk], apple-only-cpu-tunables, non-apple-core-type-header, non-apple-cache-monitor,
non-apple-iommu-bootstrap, zzx-pmap-sync-64bit-pa, native-verbose-console, native-dt-panic-region),
commit 68c5134. License: BSD-2-Clause-Patent, Copyright (c) 2026, UniXNU contributors (text in
docs/ios26-port-status.md, section Licenses).

